<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Practical decoding: <math id="S4.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-tie breaking</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proxy robustness.</span>
When <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained from scalable proxy scorers rather than i.i.d. human samples, a uniform proxy-error assumption yields a robust LCB guarantee; we defer the formal statement and proof to Appendix <a href="#A1.SS12" title="A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-rule as a constrained optimization.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-tie-breaking is equivalent to</p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}(s)\in\arg\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\max}(s)-\epsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}(s)\in\arg\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\max}(s)-\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\max}(s):=\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\max}(s):=\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Pareto view.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ ϵ-rule as a constrained optimization. ‣ 4.2 Practical decoding: ϵ-tie breaking ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) selects a Pareto-optimal point of the robust-value–disagreement trade-off: among candidates whose robust value is within <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of the best, it returns the least controversial one.
Moreover, when the chosen point is <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">supported</em>, the same solution can be written as a scalarization
<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{y}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{y}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
formal statements and proofs are deferred to Appendix <a href="#A1.SS13" title="A.13 ϵ-tie breaking: Pareto and scalarization properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Two-stage rule.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid sacrificing entropic value excessively for marginal robustness, we use:</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\mid\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\max}(s)-\epsilon\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\mid\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\max}(s)-\epsilon\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{\epsilon}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{\epsilon}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\arg\min_{y\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\arg\min_{y\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)}\widehat{\sigma}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This approximates the scalarized decoder <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{y}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{y}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)</annotation></semantics></math> by enforcing near-optimality in entropic value and then selecting the least controversial candidate.
In practice, we tune all risk parameters (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\tau,\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\tau,\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) on a held-out development set; detailed tuning protocols are provided in Appendix <a href="#A8.SS4" title="H.4 Selecting risk controls and practical calibration ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Multi-scorer robustness</h3>

<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scorer-robust decoding (multi-reward models).</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In scalable proxy settings, satisfaction scores may come from learned reward models and be sensitive to model shift or proxy over-optimization.
We optionally hedge this <em id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">scorer ambiguity</em> by using a family of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> scorers indexed by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each candidate <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, scorer <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> provides <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> scalar samples <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{m,i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{m,i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., via perturbations), from which we compute the scorer-specific entropic value <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and risk premium <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because reward scales can differ across scorers, we apply a per-prompt affine normalization (Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Scorer ambiguity and multi-scorer aggregation ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).
We then aggregate scorer-specific entropic values using a soft worst-case operator:</p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y):=-\frac{1}{\gamma}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\!\big(-\gamma\,\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)\big)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y):=-\frac{1}{\gamma}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\!\big(-\gamma\,\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)\big)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and aggregate risk premia pessimistically by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We decode by maximizing <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> subject to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (or its penalized form).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Scorer aggregation as KL-regularized DRO over scorers)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{m}:=\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{m}:=\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=(1/M,\ldots,1/M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=(1/M,\ldots,1/M)</annotation></semantics></math> and the simplex <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{M}:=\{\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}_{+}:\sum_{m=1}^{M}q_{m}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{M}:=\{\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}_{+}:\sum_{m=1}^{M}q_{m}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the soft worst-case aggregation (<a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Scorer-robust decoding (multi-reward models). ‣ 4.3 Multi-scorer robustness ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) admits the variational form</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)=\inf_{\mathbf{q}\in\Delta_{M}}\left\{\sum_{m=1}^{M}q_{m}v_{m}+\frac{1}{\gamma}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbf{q}\|\mathbf{u})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)=\inf_{\mathbf{q}\in\Delta_{M}}\left\{\sum_{m=1}^{M}q_{m}v_{m}+\frac{1}{\gamma}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbf{q}\|\mathbf{u})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. (<a href="#S4.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Proposition 4.1 (Scorer aggregation as KL-regularized DRO over scorers). ‣ Scorer-robust decoding (multi-reward models). ‣ 4.3 Multi-scorer robustness ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>) shows that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> interpolates between averaging across scorers (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\!\to\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\!\to\!0</annotation></semantics></math>) and a worst-case scorer (<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\!\to\!\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\!\to\!\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), yielding a principled hedge against scorer shift. In particular, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{m}v_{m}\leq\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\leq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m}v_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{m}v_{m}\leq\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\leq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m}v_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing in <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiment</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup and Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Candidate sets and evaluation protocol.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we generate a fixed candidate pool <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (shared across all methods),
so differences arise solely from the inference-time <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">selection rule</em>.
In the human-grounded setting, for each <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> we collect <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> scalar satisfaction ratings
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Christiano et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Stiennon et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>,
and split annotators into disjoint selection and evaluation sets
<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid selection–evaluation leakage.
All decoders operate on statistics computed from <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our entropic decoder uses the empirical entropic value in the human-grounded setting (where <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}=\widehat{V}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}=\widehat{V}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and uses the scorer-robust aggregated value <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> (and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>) in proxy settings with multiple reward models.
Second-moment baselines use only <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y),\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y),\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y))</annotation></semantics></math> (or their scorer-indexed analogues under proxies).
All reported metrics are computed on held-out ratings in <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> (definitions in Appendix <a href="#A8.SS3" title="H.3 Complete metric definitions and computation ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Estimating mean and disagreement.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> as the mean and disagreement estimates, derived from either empirical samples or scorer proxies .
DARC is <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">inference-time only</em>, modifying the selection over <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> without retraining.
While our theory assumes multi-annotator feedback, we validate proxy uncertainty as a scalable approximation for human disagreement.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proxies, baselines, and hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When multi-rater human scores are unavailable, we use scalable proxy scorers (e.g., ensembles / bootstrap reward models)
to obtain a proxy mean together with either (i) a score distribution for computing <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, or
(ii) a proxy disagreement diagnostic <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\text{proxy}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>proxy</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\text{proxy}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kendall and Gal, 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lakshminarayanan et al., 2017</a>)</cite>;
we validate proxy–human alignment via rank correlation and stratified analyses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Uma et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
Inference-time baselines include mean Best-of-<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>,
inference-time hedging methods for reward hacking (Best-of-Poisson and HedgeTune) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khalaf et al., 2025</a>)</cite>,
pessimistic best-of-<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> reranking via an auxiliary error/atypicality model (<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Caution</em>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anonymous, 2025</a>)</cite>,
uncertainty-based reranking (e.g., MC-Dropout) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gal and Ghahramani, 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kendall and Gal, 2017</a>)</cite>,
reward-regularized decoding (RBoN) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jinnai et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">DeAL</em> (top-<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> lookahead reward-guided decoding) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>;
training-time baselines include cDPO/rDPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mitchell, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chowdhury et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
We report default settings and full tuning ranges (including our LCB- and DRO-instantiated decoding rules),
along with complete baseline configurations and implementation details,
in Appendix <a href="#A8.SS2" title="H.2 Hyperparameter selection ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.2</span></a> (see also Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Detailed decoding rules and baselines ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference overhead.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Disagreement estimation adds only a modest inference-time cost: in our implementation, using <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}=4/8/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}=4/8/16</annotation></semantics></math> increases end-to-end latency by only <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 1.5\%/2.0\%/3.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>2.0</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>3.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 1.5\%/2.0\%/3.2\%</annotation></semantics></math>, since candidate generation dominates runtime (Appendix <a href="#A8.SS6" title="H.6 Inference latency. ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.6</span></a>, Table <a href="#A8.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ H.6 Inference latency. ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics (mean, risk, and tail).</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and candidate response <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, we evaluate rewards on a held-out rater set <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> and report the empirical mean <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
As a scalable proxy for robustness, we compute a <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">perturbation-sensitivity</em> statistic <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as the standard deviation of rewards across <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math> style-preserving perturbations of <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>
(see Appendix <a href="#A8.SS13" title="H.13 Style-preserving perturbations for disagreement estimation ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.13</span></a>).
Human evaluation details are in Appendix <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Human Evaluation Protocol and Annotator Quality Controls ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>; the human mean is the average rating and the human variance is the sample variance across raters.
We summarize performance via <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{\text{eval}}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{\text{eval}}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, using the same <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for all methods (Appendix <a href="#A8.SS14" title="H.14 Tradeoff metric weight: choice and sensitivity ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.14</span></a>).
We also report <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}</annotation></semantics></math> over prompts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chow et al., 2015</a>)</cite>; see Appendix <a href="#A8.SS3" title="H.3 Complete metric definitions and computation ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.08145v1/ablation_icml_final.svg" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/96;" width="476" height="96"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.F2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation Studies.<span id="S5.F2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Impact of key hyperparameters on risk mitigation performance.
</span>(a)<span id="S5.F2.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Candidate pool size <math id="S5.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>(b)<span id="S5.F2.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Risk sensitivity coefficient <math id="S5.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>(c)<span id="S5.F2.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Constraint threshold <math id="S5.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span>(d)<span id="S5.F2.9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Perturbation budget <math id="S5.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
