<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Theoretical Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>A self-normalized (empirical-variance) concentration bound</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first record a standard empirical-Bernstein style inequality (a self-normalized concentration bound)
that controls the deviation of the empirical mean in terms of the empirical standard deviation.
This lemma is used to prove Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Empirical Bernstein bound (bounded case))<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. supported on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i},\qquad\hat{\sigma}^{2}:=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\hat{\mu})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i},\qquad\hat{\sigma}^{2}:=\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\hat{\mu})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\geq\hat{\mu}-\sqrt{\frac{2\hat{\sigma}^{2}\log(2/\delta)}{n}}-\frac{7(b-a)\log(2/\delta)}{3(n-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\geq\hat{\mu}-\sqrt{\frac{2\hat{\sigma}^{2}\log(2/\delta)}{n}}-\frac{7(b-a)\log(2/\delta)}{3(n-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Empirical Bernstein bound (bounded case)). ‣ A.1 A self-normalized (empirical-variance) concentration bound ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> is a standard form of empirical Bernstein inequality.
We use it because it yields the same structure as (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>):
a leading term of order <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}\sqrt{\log(1/\delta)/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}\sqrt{\log(1/\delta)/n}</annotation></semantics></math> and a lower-order term of order <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
For completeness, we provide a short proof outline in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS7" title="A.7 Proof outline for Lemma ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof outline.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We apply an empirical-Bernstein (self-normalized) inequality for bounded random variables to each fixed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>,
then take a union bound over <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> candidates with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K</annotation></semantics></math>.
An alternative derivation can be obtained from Freedman’s martingale inequality.
We then track constants to obtain (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix any <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and apply Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Empirical Bernstein bound (bounded case)). ‣ A.1 A self-normalized (empirical-variance) concentration bound ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{i}(y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{i}(y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K</annotation></semantics></math>.
With probability at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta^{\prime})}{n}}-\frac{7(b-a)\log(2/\delta^{\prime})}{3(n-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta^{\prime})}{n}}-\frac{7(b-a)\log(2/\delta^{\prime})}{3(n-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking a union bound over the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> candidates yields probability at least <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> that the inequality holds for all <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, note that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(2/\delta^{\prime})=\log(2K/\delta)\leq\log(K/\delta)+\log 2\leq C_{0}\,\log(K/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(2/\delta^{\prime})=\log(2K/\delta)\leq\log(K/\delta)+\log 2\leq C_{0}\,\log(K/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for a universal constant <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (we may assume <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/\delta\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/\delta\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise the bound is trivial).
Moreover, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n-1}\leq\frac{2}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n-1}\leq\frac{2}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Absorbing these constant factors into a single universal <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> yields (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>From LCB decoding to mean–dispersion decoding</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix formalizes the “ignoring constants / lower-order term” step used to connect uniform LCB maximization to a <em id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">mean–dispersion surrogate</em> (used as an ablation / efficient approximation), rather than as the defining objective of our primary KL-robust entropic decoder.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mean–dispersion surrogate form under bounded ratings)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the conditions of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y):=\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y):=\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then any maximizer of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is also a maximizer of</span></p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y),\qquad\lambda:=c\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y),\qquad\lambda:=c\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">since the last term <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\,(b-a)\log(K/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\,(b-a)\log(K/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The two objectives differ by an additive constant that does not depend on <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, hence they have identical argmax sets.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Standard deviation vs. Variance penalization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note a structural distinction between the LCB-derived surrogate and the entropic objective. The LCB rule (Eq. <a href="#A1.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Corollary A.2 (Mean–dispersion surrogate form under bounded ratings). ‣ A.3 From LCB decoding to mean–dispersion decoding ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) implies a penalty on the <em id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">standard deviation</em> <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> (scaling as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math>), which accounts for finite-sample estimation uncertainty. In contrast, the entropic objective (Eq. 1) approximates a mean-variance form <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}-\frac{\beta}{2}\hat{\sigma}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}-\frac{\beta}{2}\hat{\sigma}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> under Taylor expansion, reflecting intrinsic risk aversion.
While theoretically distinct, both objectives penalize dispersion. We use the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-based LCB form primarily to establish finite-sample consistency guarantees, while the entropic form serves as our primary method for capturing risk sensitivity. Empirically, both metrics effectively demote high-disagreement candidates.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix supports the statement in Section 3.1 that an analogous LCB holds under sub-Gaussian noise
(as an alternative to Assumption 3.2). We first recall a lower-tail bound for a single sub-Gaussian variable,
then derive a <em id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniform-in-<math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math></em> empirical LCB for the mean <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples, analogous to
Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounded <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> sub-Gaussian.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under boundedness <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, Hoeffding’s lemma implies <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian with
<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\leq(b-a)/2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\leq(b-a)/2.</annotation></semantics></math>
Applying Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (Sub-Gaussian lower-tail bound). ‣ Bounded ⇒ sub-Gaussian. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=(b-a)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=(b-a)/2</annotation></semantics></math> yields the bounded lower-tail bound:</p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(X\leq\mathbb{E}[X]-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{(b-a)^{2}}\right),\qquad\forall\,t&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(X\leq\mathbb{E}[X]-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{2t^{2}}{(b-a)^{2}}\right),\qquad\forall\,t&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This justifies the statement that dispersion controls conservative (lower-tail) outcomes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sub-Gaussian lower-tail bound)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian, then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(X\leq\mathbb{E}[X]-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\nu^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(X\leq\mathbb{E}[X]-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\nu^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Chernoff’s method, for any <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(X-\mathbb{E}[X]\leq-t)=\Pr(e^{-\lambda(X-\mathbb{E}[X])}\geq e^{\lambda t})\leq e^{-\lambda t}\mathbb{E}[e^{-\lambda(X-\mathbb{E}[X])}]\leq e^{-\lambda t}e^{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(X-\mathbb{E}[X]\leq-t)=\Pr(e^{-\lambda(X-\mathbb{E}[X])}\geq e^{\lambda t})\leq e^{-\lambda t}\mathbb{E}[e^{-\lambda(X-\mathbb{E}[X])}]\leq e^{-\lambda t}e^{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Optimize over <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> by setting <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=t/\nu^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=t/\nu^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to get (<a href="#A1.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Lemma A.4 (Sub-Gaussian lower-tail bound). ‣ Bounded ⇒ sub-Gaussian. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uniform empirical LCB for sub-Gaussian rewards.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a state <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and a finite candidate set <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=|\mathcal{Y}(s)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=|\mathcal{Y}(s)|</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}(y),\dots,R_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}(y),\dots,R_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. draws of the (scalar) reward with mean
<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y):=\mathbb{E}[R(y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y):=\mathbb{E}[R(y)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the empirical mean and (uncentered) empirical variance proxy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(y):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{i}(y),\qquad\hat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}(y):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bigl(R_{i}(y)-\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(y):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{i}(y),\qquad\hat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}(y):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bigl(R_{i}(y)-\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">(Any definition of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> used in the main text can be substituted here; only its nonnegativity is used below.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sub-Gaussian rewards (alternative to boundedness))<span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, the centered reward <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(y)-\mu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(y)-\mu(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian, i.e.,
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\exp(\lambda(R(y)-\mu(y)))]\leq\exp(\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\exp(\lambda(R(y)-\mu(y)))]\leq\exp(\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}/2)</annotation></semantics></math>
for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sample mean is sub-Gaussian)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption A.5 (Sub-Gaussian rewards (alternative to boundedness)). ‣ Uniform empirical LCB for sub-Gaussian rewards. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, for any fixed <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, the sample mean satisfies that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu/\sqrt{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu/\sqrt{n})</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(\lambda(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y))\right)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n}\right),\qquad\forall\,\lambda\in\mathbb{R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(\lambda(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y))\right)\right]\leq\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n}\right),\qquad\forall\,\lambda\in\mathbb{R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Identical to the standard argument: by independence and the sub-Gaussian MGF bound,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[e^{\lambda(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y))}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda}{n}(R_{i}(y)-\mu(y))\right)\right]\leq\prod_{i=1}^{n}\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[e^{\lambda(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\mu(y))}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda}{n}(R_{i}(y)-\mu(y))\right)\right]\leq\prod_{i=1}^{n}\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n^{2}}\right)=\exp\!\left(\frac{\lambda^{2}\nu^{2}}{2n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform sub-Gaussian LCB (analogue of Prop. <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>))<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists an absolute constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,
simultaneously for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\nu\,\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\nu\,\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We denote the right-hand side by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}^{\mathrm{subG}}_{\delta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi><mi>subG</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}^{\mathrm{subG}}_{\delta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma A.6 (Sample mean is sub-Gaussian). ‣ Uniform empirical LCB for sub-Gaussian rewards. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma A.4 (Sub-Gaussian lower-tail bound). ‣ Bounded ⇒ sub-Gaussian. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>, for any <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\leq\mu(y)-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{nt^{2}}{2\nu^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\leq\mu(y)-t\right)\leq\exp\!\left(-\frac{nt^{2}}{2\nu^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\nu\sqrt{2\log(K/\delta)/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\nu\sqrt{2\log(K/\delta)/n}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\mu(y)&lt;\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\nu\sqrt{\frac{2\log(K/\delta)}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{\delta}{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\mu(y)&lt;\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\nu\sqrt{\frac{2\log(K/\delta)}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{\delta}{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying a union bound over all <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> yields that with probability at least <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,
(<a href="#A1.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proposition A.7 (Uniform sub-Gaussian LCB (analogue of Prop. )). ‣ Uniform empirical LCB for sub-Gaussian rewards. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) holds simultaneously for all <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>. Absorb the factor <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into an absolute constant <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion (relation to Prop. <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition A.7 (Uniform sub-Gaussian LCB (analogue of Prop. )). ‣ Uniform empirical LCB for sub-Gaussian rewards. ‣ A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> provides the claimed uniform LCB under sub-Gaussian noise.
Compared to the bounded-rewards LCB in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), the sub-Gaussian LCB replaces the empirical
dispersion term <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and the boundedness-dependent lower-order correction
<math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(b-a)\log(K/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(b-a)\log(K/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math> with the (known) sub-Gaussian scale <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
If one additionally wants a data-dependent (empirical-Bernstein/Freedman-type) bound under sub-Gaussianity,
one can combine sub-exponential concentration for <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R(y)-\mu(y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R(y)-\mu(y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with a union bound; we omit this here
since Section 3.1 only requires existence of an analogous LCB.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (KL-robust value equals an entropic objective). ‣ KL-robust (entropic) decoding. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The equivalence between the KL-robust value and the entropic risk measure is a classical result in the theory of risk-sensitive control and large deviations, often referred to as the Donsker-Varadhan variational formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dupuis and Ellis, 2011</a>)</cite>. We provide the derivation here for completeness.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the definition of the KL-regularized robust value given in Equation (<a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ KL-robust (entropic) decoding. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Rob}^{\mathrm{KL}}_{\beta}(\mathbb{P};R):=\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]+\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbb{Q}\|\mathbb{P})\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Rob</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Rob}^{\mathrm{KL}}_{\beta}(\mathbb{P};R):=\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}}\left\{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]+\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbb{Q}\|\mathbb{P})\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the Radon-Nikodym derivative (density ratio). The optimization problem can be formulated as minimizing the functional <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(f)</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the normalization constraint <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f\,d\mathbb{P}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f\,d\mathbb{P}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and non-negativity <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(f)=\int f(x)R(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}\int f(x)\log f(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(f)=\int f(x)R(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}\int f(x)\log f(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">We introduce a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> for the constraint <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f\,d\mathbb{P}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f\,d\mathbb{P}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The Lagrangian is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(f,\gamma)=\int\left(f(x)R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}f(x)\log f(x)-\gamma f(x)\right)d\mathbb{P}(x)+\gamma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(f,\gamma)=\int\left(f(x)R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}f(x)\log f(x)-\gamma f(x)\right)d\mathbb{P}(x)+\gamma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the functional derivative with respect to <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and setting it to zero yields the first-order condition:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(\log f(x)+1)-\gamma=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(\log f(x)+1)-\gamma=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Solving for <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the form of the optimal twisted distribution:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log f^{*}(x)=\beta\gamma-1-\beta R(x)\implies f^{*}(x)\propto\exp(-\beta R(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log f^{*}(x)=\beta\gamma-1-\beta R(x)\implies f^{*}(x)\propto\exp(-\beta R(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Using the normalization constraint <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int f^{*}(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int f^{*}(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we determine the normalization constant (partition function) <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z:=\int\exp(-\beta R(x))\,d\mathbb{P}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[\exp(-\beta R)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=\int\exp(-\beta R(x))\,d\mathbb{P}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[\exp(-\beta R)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the optimal density ratio is given by Gibbs measure form <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}(x)=\frac{1}{Z}\exp(-\beta R(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}(x)=\frac{1}{Z}\exp(-\beta R(x))</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="A1.SS5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> back into the objective function, the expectation term and the entropy term combine conveniently:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}^{*}}[R]+\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbb{Q}^{*}\|\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}^{*}}[R]+\frac{1}{\beta}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mathbb{Q}^{*}\|\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}\log f^{*}(x)\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}\log f^{*}(x)\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(-\beta R(x)-\log Z)\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(-\beta R(x)-\log Z)\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)-R(x)-\frac{1}{\beta}\log Z\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int f^{*}(x)\left(R(x)-R(x)-\frac{1}{\beta}\log Z\right)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log Z\underbrace{\int f^{*}(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mn>1</mn></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log Z\underbrace{\int f^{*}(x)\,d\mathbb{P}(x)}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[\exp(-\beta R)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[\exp(-\beta R)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Constraint vs. penalty: Lagrangian view (finite candidate set)</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix supports the “two interchangeable controls” claim in the main text
for the entropic-risk-premium formulation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pareto optimality and (supported) scalarization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and define the entropic risk premium
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}(y)-\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}(y)-\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\beta}:=\{(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y),\hat{\mu}(y)):y\in\mathcal{Y}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\beta}:=\{(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y),\hat{\mu}(y)):y\in\mathcal{Y}\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">be a finite set.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\hat{\mu}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\hat{\mu}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is Pareto-optimal with respect to the bi-criteria
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta},\hat{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta},\hat{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., there is no <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}(y)\geq\hat{\mu}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}(y)\geq\hat{\mu}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> with at least one strict).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Conversely, if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(y^{\star}),\hat{\mu}(y^{\star}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(y^{\star}),\hat{\mu}(y^{\star}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">supported</em> Pareto-optimal point of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>
(i.e., it lies on the upper boundary of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{P}_{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{P}_{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math> and admits a supporting line),
then there exists <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\hat{\mu}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\hat{\mu}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is a standard scalarization fact for finite bi-criteria optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Boyd and Vandenberghe, 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Miettinen, 1999</a>)</cite>.
If a solution were dominated under <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{RP}^{c}_{\beta},\hat{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>RP</mi><mi>β</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{RP}^{c}_{\beta},\hat{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math>, it could not maximize any nonnegative linear scalarization.
Conversely, each supported Pareto-optimal point admits a supporting hyperplane for <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{P}_{\beta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{P}_{\beta})</annotation></semantics></math>, whose slope yields a <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes <math id="A1.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}-\lambda\,\mathrm{RP}\textperiodcentered_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>RP</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>·</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}-\lambda\,\mathrm{RP}\textperiodcentered_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Proof outline for Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Empirical Bernstein bound (bounded case)). ‣ A.1 A self-normalized (empirical-variance) concentration bound ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly outline the proof strategy for Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Empirical Bernstein bound (bounded case)). ‣ A.1 A self-normalized (empirical-variance) concentration bound ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One route is to apply a martingale concentration inequality (Freedman/Bernstein-type) to the centered sum
<math id="A1.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> and control the conditional variance by the empirical variance, yielding an “empirical Bernstein” bound.
Another route is to invoke a known empirical Bernstein theorem directly.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.8 </span>Selection statistics: empirical mean, dispersion, and CVaR</h3>

<div id="A1.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each input <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and candidate response <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, we estimate robust selection statistics using a fixed reward model <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Concretely, we construct <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> style-preserving perturbations <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{y}^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{y}^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., formatting or phrasing variations),
and compute <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> reward samples
<math id="A1.SS8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(m)}(s,y)=R_{\psi}(s,\tilde{y}^{(m)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(m)}(s,y)=R_{\psi}(s,\tilde{y}^{(m)}).</annotation></semantics></math>
We then define:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}r^{(m)}(s,y),\qquad\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)=\sqrt{\frac{1}{M-1}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\big(r^{(m)}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)\big)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}r^{(m)}(s,y),\qquad\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)=\sqrt{\frac{1}{M-1}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\big(r^{(m)}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)\big)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For CVaR, let <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r^{(1:M)}_{(1)}\leq\cdots\leq r^{(1:M)}_{(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(1:M)}_{(1)}\leq\cdots\leq r^{(1:M)}_{(M)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sorted reward samples, and let
<math id="A1.SS8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\max\{1,\lceil\alpha M\rceil\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\max\{1,\lceil\alpha M\rceil\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use the empirical lower-tail mean</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{CVaR}}_{\alpha,\text{sel}}(s,y)=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}r^{(1:M)}_{(i)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CVaR</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>sel</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{CVaR}}_{\alpha,\text{sel}}(s,y)=\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}r^{(1:M)}_{(i)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In all experiments, <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed globally (no per-task tuning), and the same reward model <math id="A1.SS8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> is used for all methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.9 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the lower bound (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and characterize when it is tight.
Let <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> constraint implies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]=D_{\chi^{2}}(\mathbb{Q}\,\|\,\mathbb{P})\leq\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]=D_{\chi^{2}}(\mathbb{Q}\,\|\,\mathbb{P})\leq\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(1+g)R]=\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(1+g)R]=\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By Cauchy–Schwarz,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]\geq-\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]}\ \sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})^{2}]}\geq-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]\geq-\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]}\ \sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})^{2}]}\geq-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Taking the infimum over all feasible <math id="A1.SS9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> yields (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For tightness, equality in Cauchy–Schwarz is achieved when</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}(R)=-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}(R)=-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which corresponds to the candidate extremal density</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)=1+g^{\star}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)=1+g^{\star}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS9.p2.3" class="ltx_p">i.e., (<a href="#A2.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ B.2 Tightness and the extremal density ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean) ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>).
This defines a valid probability density if it is nonnegative <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost surely, which is exactly the stated condition.
A sufficient condition is <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}/\sqrt{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}/\sqrt{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS9.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>-a.s., giving (<a href="#A2.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ B.2 Tightness and the extremal density ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean) ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Specializing to the empirical distribution <math id="A1.SS9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}</annotation></semantics></math> yields (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) by substituting
<math id="A1.SS9.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS9.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\sqrt{\widehat{v}_{n}(y)}=\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\sqrt{\widehat{v}_{n}(y)}=\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma A.11 (ϵ-tie breaking on the robust-value–disagreement frontier). ‣ A.13 ϵ-tie breaking: Pareto and scalarization properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> be any solution of (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ ϵ-rule as a constrained optimization. ‣ 4.2 Practical decoding: ϵ-tie breaking ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>).
If there existed <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> with at least one strict inequality, then:
- if <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)&gt;\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)&gt;\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible for (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ ϵ-rule as a constrained optimization. ‣ 4.2 Practical decoding: ϵ-tie breaking ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) and strictly better in the objective <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>;
- if <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)=\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)=\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}(s,y)&lt;\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}(s,y)&lt;\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is also feasible and strictly better.
Either case contradicts optimality of <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A1.SS10.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is Pareto-optimal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the scalarization claim, consider the finite set</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}:=\{(\hat{\sigma}(s,y),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)):\ y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}:=\{(\hat{\sigma}(s,y),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)):\ y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS10.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and its convex hull <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon}),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon}),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a supported Pareto-optimal point, then there exists a supporting line to <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>conv</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{conv}(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math>
with outward normal <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{\epsilon},1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{\epsilon},1)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})\quad\forall\,y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})\quad\forall\,y\in\mathcal{Y}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS10.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore <math id="A1.SS10.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes the linear scalarization, proving (<a href="#A1.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Lemma A.11 (ϵ-tie breaking on the robust-value–disagreement frontier). ‣ A.13 ϵ-tie breaking: Pareto and scalarization properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.11 </span>Second-moment surrogate of the LCB rule</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Second-moment surrogate)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Up to an additive term uniform across <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, maximizing <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{LCB}}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\Big(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\Big),\qquad\lambda:=c\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>LCB</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{LCB}}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\Big(\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\Big),\qquad\lambda:=c\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.12 </span>Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates</h3>

<div id="A1.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix formalizes robustness of LCB-based selection when the decoder uses proxy estimates
<math id="A1.SS12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\mu},\tilde{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mu},\tilde{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> in place of the empirical statistics <math id="A1.SS12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mu}_{n},\hat{\sigma}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mu}_{n},\hat{\sigma}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We show that under a uniform proxy error event, proxy maximization incurs only an additive slack
<math id="A1.SS12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math> relative to the sample-based optimum.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Assumption (uniform proxy closeness).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{\mu}(y),\tilde{\sigma}(y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{\mu}(y),\tilde{\sigma}(y))</annotation></semantics></math> be proxy estimates used by the decoder.
Assume that with probability at least <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{\mathrm{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{\mathrm{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\tilde{\mu}(y)-\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\big|\leq\varepsilon_{\mu},\qquad\big|\tilde{\sigma}(y)-\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\big|\leq\varepsilon_{\sigma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\tilde{\mu}(y)-\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\big|\leq\varepsilon_{\mu},\qquad\big|\tilde{\sigma}(y)-\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\big|\leq\varepsilon_{\sigma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark (dependence and interpretation).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption (<a href="#A1.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Assumption (uniform proxy closeness). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) intentionally abstracts away the dependence structure of proxy-generated scores:
the perturbation-and-RM procedure may induce correlated errors and systematic bias.
Our goal here is not to claim that proxy samples satisfy i.i.d. concentration, but to show that <em id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">any</em> proxy
estimator that is uniformly close to the sample statistics yields only an additive degradation in the pessimistic value,
captured by <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In Sec. 4, we empirically assess the accuracy of the proxy estimates and their correlation with human disagreement.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robust LCB under proxy errors)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the intersection of the LCB event in Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (proved in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>)
and the proxy error event (<a href="#A1.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Assumption (uniform proxy closeness). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), simultaneously for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)\;\geq\;\underbrace{\tilde{\mu}(y)-c\,\tilde{\sigma}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}_{\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)}\;-\;\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>LCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)\;\geq\;\underbrace{\tilde{\mu}(y)-c\,\tilde{\sigma}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}_{\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)}\;-\;\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}:=\varepsilon_{\mu}+c\,\varepsilon_{\sigma}\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}:=\varepsilon_{\mu}+c\,\varepsilon_{\sigma}\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The intersection event holds with probability at least <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-(\delta+\delta_{\mathrm{prox}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-(\delta+\delta_{\mathrm{prox}})</annotation></semantics></math> by a union bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, letting <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>LCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have the value suboptimality bound</span></p>
<table id="A1.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y^{\star})-\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(\tilde{y})\;\leq\;2\,\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y^{\star})-\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(\tilde{y})\;\leq\;2\,\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, proxy maximization is within <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}})</annotation></semantics></math> of the sample-based optimum.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (proved in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>),
for all <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> on the LCB event,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)\geq\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,(b-a)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#A1.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Assumption (uniform proxy closeness). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we have <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\geq\tilde{\mu}(y)-\varepsilon_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(y)\geq\tilde{\mu}(y)-\varepsilon_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\leq\tilde{\sigma}(y)+\varepsilon_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\leq\tilde{\sigma}(y)+\varepsilon_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting and rearranging yields (<a href="#A1.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Corollary A.10 (Robust LCB under proxy errors). ‣ Remark (dependence and interpretation). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>)–(<a href="#A1.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ Corollary A.10 (Robust LCB under proxy errors). ‣ Remark (dependence and interpretation). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, since for all <math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> we have
<math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)\geq\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)-\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>LCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)\geq\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)-\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A1.SS12.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)\leq\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)+\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>LCB</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>prox</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LCB}_{\delta}(y)\leq\widetilde{\mathrm{LCB}}_{\delta}(y)+\Delta_{\mathrm{prox}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
standard argmax stability yields (<a href="#A1.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Corollary A.10 (Robust LCB under proxy errors). ‣ Remark (dependence and interpretation). ‣ A.12 Robustness to proxy disagreement estimates ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.13 </span><math id="A1.SS13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-tie breaking: Pareto and scalarization properties</h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-tie breaking on the robust-value–disagreement frontier)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a prompt <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and candidate set <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any solution <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> of  (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ ϵ-rule as a constrained optimization. ‣ 4.2 Practical decoding: ϵ-tie breaking ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) is Pareto-optimal with respect to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{V}_{\beta},\hat{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{V}_{\beta},\hat{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math>:
there does not exist <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\leq\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> with at least one strict inequality.
Moreover, if <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon}),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon}),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math> is a <em id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">supported</em> Pareto-optimal point of the finite set
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\hat{\sigma}(s,y),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)):y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\hat{\sigma}(s,y),\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)):y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then there exists a (possibly non-unique) <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\epsilon}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}(s)\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}(s)\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda_{\epsilon}\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS13.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">See Appendix <a href="#A1.SS10" title="A.10 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(<math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-rule approximates <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>–dispersion under small robust-value gaps)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and let
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\lambda}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\lambda}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\big(\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\lambda}\in\mathcal{F}_{\epsilon}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., its robust value is within <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> of the best robust value),
then the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-tie-break output <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\lambda})-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\lambda})-\epsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\epsilon})-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\epsilon})\geq\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y_{\lambda})-\lambda\hat{\sigma}(s,y_{\lambda})-\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.14 </span>From pairwise comparisons to scalar samples</h3>

<section id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">From pairwise preferences to scalar satisfaction (estimation layer).</h4>

<div id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Human feedback is often collected as pairwise comparisons or multi-criteria judgments rather than scalar scores.
One may induce scalar satisfaction via standard latent-utility scalarizations (e.g., Bradley–Terry/Thurstone-style fitting or calibrated ratings); our method then operates on the induced scalar samples.
We emphasize that the <em id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high-probability guarantee</em> in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> applies directly to the i.i.d. scalar-sample regime above; when scalarization is obtained indirectly from comparisons, we treat the resulting <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\mu},\hat{\sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> as an estimator and validate it empirically.
We sketch how common pairwise preference data can be mapped to scalar samples used in Sec. <a href="#S3" title="3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Assume annotator <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has a latent utility <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> and pairwise labels are generated from noisy utility differences,
e.g., Bradley–Terry / Thurstone:</p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr(y\succ_{i}y^{\prime})=\sigma\!\left(\frac{U_{i}(y)-U_{i}(y^{\prime})}{\eta}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mo>≻</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(y\succ_{i}y^{\prime})=\sigma\!\left(\frac{U_{i}(y)-U_{i}(y^{\prime})}{\eta}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a logistic or Gaussian CDF and <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given multiple comparisons involving <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, a scalarization (e.g., per-annotator win-rate or fitted BT/Thurstone score) yields a proxy <math id="A1.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{U}_{i}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{U}_{i}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.13</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LCB form under sub-Gaussian scalarization noise)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{U}_{i}(y)=U_{i}(y)+\xi_{i}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{U}_{i}(y)=U_{i}(y)+\xi_{i}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi_{i}(y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi_{i}(y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian.
Then with probability at least <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, simultaneously for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(y)\;\geq\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c^{\prime}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(y)\;\geq\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c^{\prime}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for an absolute constant <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (up to lower-order terms), i.e., the same mean–dispersion LCB structure as in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> (<math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO robust mean)</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Full characterization.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sufficient tightness condition is that the extremal density</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is nonnegative <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>-almost surely.
In particular, it holds if <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}/\sqrt{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}/\sqrt{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> a.s.
For bounded ratings <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, nonnegativity holds whenever <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\rho}\,(b-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})\leq\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\rho}\,(b-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})\leq\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a complete proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>. We first prove the general lower bound
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\geq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\geq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any square-integrable <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>,
and then characterize a sufficient condition for tightness. Finally, we specialize to the empirical distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>General bound via a change of measure</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}\ll\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(R):=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(R):=\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> constraint reads <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\left[\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)\,R\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}\!\left[\frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R)\,R\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(1+g(R))R]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(1+g(R))R]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[R]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)R]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)R]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By Cauchy–Schwarz,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]\geq-\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]}\ \sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})^{2}]}\geq-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g(R)(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})]\geq-\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{2}]}\ \sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})^{2}]}\geq-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Taking the infimum over all <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\geq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\mathbb{P})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\geq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">proving (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Tightness and the extremal density</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Equality in Cauchy–Schwarz holds when <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(R)</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}(R):=-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}(R):=-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{\star}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[g^{\star}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(g^{\star})^{2}]=\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}}[(g^{\star})^{2}]=\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
If additionally <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+g^{\star}(R)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+g^{\star}(R)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}</annotation></semantics></math>-a.s., we may define</p>
<table id="A2.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R):=1+g^{\star}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}{d\mathbb{P}}(R):=1+g^{\star}(R)=1-\sqrt{\rho}\,\frac{R-\mu_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is a valid Radon–Nikodym derivative.
Plugging <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> into the derivation above achieves equality, giving</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}[R]=\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}^{\star}}[R]=\mu_{\mathbb{P}}-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">A sufficient condition for nonnegativity is</p>
<table id="A2.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\frac{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sqrt{\rho}}\quad\mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ℙ</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-a.s.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leq\mu_{\mathbb{P}}+\frac{\sigma_{\mathbb{P}}}{\sqrt{\rho}}\quad\mathbb{P}\text{-a.s.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which implies <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+g^{\star}(R)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+g^{\star}(R)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> a.s.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Specialization to the empirical distribution</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}=\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\delta_{R_{i}(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}=\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\delta_{R_{i}(y)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}\ll\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>≪</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}\ll\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a probability vector <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Delta^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Delta^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> supported on the same atoms:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}\delta_{R_{i}(y)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}\delta_{R_{i}(y)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform, the <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergence becomes</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\chi^{2}}(\mathbb{Q}\|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{(q_{i}-1/n)^{2}}{1/n}=n\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(q_{i}-\frac{1}{n}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℚ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\chi^{2}}(\mathbb{Q}\|\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{(q_{i}-1/n)^{2}}{1/n}=n\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(q_{i}-\frac{1}{n}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}R_{i}(y),\quad\mu_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y),\quad\sigma_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}^{2}=\widehat{v}_{n}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{i}R_{i}(y),\quad\mu_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y),\quad\sigma_{\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}}^{2}=\widehat{v}_{n}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{v}_{n}(y)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(R_{i}(y)-\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{v}_{n}(y)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(R_{i}(y)-\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, whenever the empirical nonnegativity condition holds on the support,
the worst-case mean equals the closed form</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sqrt{\widehat{v}_{n}(y)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]=\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\sqrt{\rho}\,\sqrt{\widehat{v}_{n}(y)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Otherwise, the lower bound (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) still holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(Conservative approximation under gap)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When the nonnegativity condition (<a href="#A2.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ B.2 Tightness and the extremal density ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean) ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) is violated (e.g., due to outliers far below the mean or large <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>), the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality implies that the closed form <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\sqrt{\rho}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\sqrt{\rho}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a strict <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">lower bound</em> on the true <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO objective.
In this regime, maximizing the mean–dispersion surrogate effectively optimizes a quantity that is <em id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">more conservative</em> than the exact distributionally robust mean. This aligns with our overall goal of pessimistic selection: the surrogate does not overstate the robust value even when the local approximation is inexact.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Calibrating LCB scaling to <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO radius</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix formalizes a <em id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">numerical calibration</em> between the LCB penalty in
Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> and the ambiguity radius in empirical <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO.
Importantly, this calibration is <em id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> meant to claim that LCB and DRO model the same source of uncertainty:
LCB controls <em id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">finite-sample estimation uncertainty</em> for <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO is commonly interpreted
as <em id="A3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distributional/aleatoric</em> robustness. Here we use <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO as a convenient <em id="A3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">variational
reparameterization</em> of the same mean–dispersion functional, which yields an interpretable radius <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>
corresponding to a chosen standard-deviation penalty <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exact <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> mapping for empirical <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a candidate <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and its empirical distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume the nonnegativity condition in Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> holds on the empirical support.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\;=\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\rho}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y),\qquad\lambda_{\rho}:=\sqrt{\rho}\,\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>ρ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\;=\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\rho}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y),\qquad\lambda_{\rho}:=\sqrt{\rho}\,\sqrt{\tfrac{n-1}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Equivalently, for a desired penalty <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, choosing</span></p>
<table id="A3.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\lambda):=\frac{n}{n-1}\,\lambda^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\lambda):=\frac{n}{n-1}\,\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">makes the empirical <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO robust mean exactly equal to <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Beyond the nonnegativity regime.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The equality in (<a href="#A3.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Proposition C.1 (Exact 𝜆–𝜌 mapping for empirical 𝜒^2-DRO). ‣ Appendix C Calibrating LCB scaling to 𝜒^2-DRO radius ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) requires a sufficient nonnegativity condition
(Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>). When this condition fails (e.g., due to heavy-tailed empirical support or large <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>),
the closed-form expression may no longer be tight. Nevertheless, Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Proposition 3.6 (𝜒^2-DRO robust mean admits a mean–dispersion form). ‣ 𝜒^2-DRO yields a mean–dispersion special case. ‣ 3.2 Distributional risk: DRO characterizations of pessimistic value ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> still provides the
<em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">conservative lower bound</em></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\;\geq\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\rho}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ℚ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\mathbb{Q}\in\mathcal{U}_{\rho}(\widehat{\mathbb{P}}_{n}^{y})}\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{Q}}[R]\;\geq\;\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\rho}\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so the mean–dispersion form remains a valid pessimistic surrogate even outside the tightness regime.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion: LCB as calibrated DRO plus lower-order slack.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> provides a uniform high-probability lower bound</p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)\geq\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,\nu(y)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}\quad\text{simultaneously for all }y\in\mathcal{Y}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>simultaneously for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)\geq\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-c\,\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}-c\,\nu(y)\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}\quad\text{simultaneously for all }y\in\mathcal{Y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\delta}:=c\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\rho_{\delta}:=\rho(\lambda_{\delta})=\frac{n}{n-1}\lambda_{\delta}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\delta}:=c\sqrt{\frac{\log(K/\delta)}{n}}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\rho_{\delta}:=\rho(\lambda_{\delta})=\frac{n}{n-1}\lambda_{\delta}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By Proposition <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition C.1 (Exact 𝜆–𝜌 mapping for empirical 𝜒^2-DRO). ‣ Appendix C Calibrating LCB scaling to 𝜒^2-DRO radius ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, in the nonnegativity regime the empirical <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-DRO robust mean under radius <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>
matches <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\delta}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{n}(y)-\lambda_{\delta}\widehat{\sigma}_{n}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> exactly.
The additional term <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\,\nu(y)\log(K/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\,\nu(y)\log(K/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite-sample slack needed to convert this robust value
into a <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">high-probability</em> lower bound on the true mean <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(y)</annotation></semantics></math> under the assumed concentration scale <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation of the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent radius.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mapping <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\delta}\propto\log(K/\delta)/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\delta}\propto\log(K/\delta)/n</annotation></semantics></math> arises because <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to control estimation error uniformly over <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> candidates.
This <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-dependence should be interpreted as an <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">estimation-calibrated</em> DRO radius: as <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the ambiguity set shrinks because the empirical mean becomes well-estimated.
However, we emphasize that in preference alignment, high empirical variance often signals intrinsic heterogeneity (disagreement) rather than pure noise.(empirically supported by the monotonic trend across disagreement buckets; see Fig <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Human-loop evaluation and tail robustness. ‣ 5.2 Results ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)
Thus, while the <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">statistical</em> radius required for concentration decays with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">functional form</em> of the penalty (i.e., penalizing dispersion) remains structurally isomorphic to a robustness constraint against disagreement.
This allows the LCB framework to serve a dual purpose: rigorously controlling finite-sample error while effectively acting as a proxy to demote controversial candidates.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>On dependence across candidates and the uniform guarantee</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our uniform guarantee in Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> does not require independence across candidates.
It only requires per-candidate concentration for each fixed <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and a union bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Union bound without independence)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}_{y}\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}_{y}\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> be any collection of events (possibly dependent).
If for each <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y})\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y})\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\left(\bigcap_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\mathcal{E}_{y}\right)\geq 1-\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y}^{c})\geq 1-K\delta^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>c</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left(\bigcap_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\mathcal{E}_{y}\right)\geq 1-\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y}^{c})\geq 1-K\delta^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=|\mathcal{Y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=|\mathcal{Y}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Application to Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each fixed <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, the self-normalized empirical-Bernstein inequality yields an event <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>
such that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y})\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\mathcal{E}_{y})\geq 1-\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and on <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> the bound (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition 3.3 (Uniform LCB). ‣ Bridge to pairwise preferences. ‣ 3.1 Estimation risk: uniform LCB and a mean–dispersion surrogate ‣ 3 Guarantees via Lower Confidence Bounds ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) holds.
Annotator overlap across different candidates can create dependence among <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{E}_{y}\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{E}_{y}\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
but Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1 (Union bound without independence). ‣ Appendix D On dependence across candidates and the uniform guarantee ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> shows that the intersection event still holds with probability at least <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-K\delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-K\delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Setting <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\delta/K</annotation></semantics></math> yields the stated uniform guarantee.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Scorer ambiguity and multi-scorer aggregation</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix details our proxy instantiation that hedges <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">scorer ambiguity</em> when scalar satisfaction samples are produced by learned reward models.
We consider a family of <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> scorers indexed by <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[M]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each prompt <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, candidate <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, and scorer <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> scalar samples
<math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{m,i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{m,i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., via independent scorer noise, style-preserving perturbations, or repeated evaluations).
All analysis conditions on the realized candidate set <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Within-prompt normalization across scorers</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reward-model outputs may differ in scale and offset across scorers; to make aggregation meaningful, we normalize per prompt.
Define the pooled mean and standard deviation under scorer <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{R}_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{R}_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{Kn}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{m,i}(s,y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{Kn}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{m,i}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{s}_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{s}_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{Kn-1}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big(R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s)\big)^{2}}\ &gt;\ 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.778em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{Kn-1}\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\big(R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s)\big)^{2}}\ &gt;\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We form normalized samples</p>
<table id="A5.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)\ :=\ \frac{R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s)}{\hat{s}_{m}(s)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)\ :=\ \frac{R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s)}{\hat{s}_{m}(s)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>, this normalization can be omitted without changing the framework.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation note.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The constants <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))</annotation></semantics></math> require access to all candidates <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for the given prompt <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
In Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ F.1 Full pseudocode for DARC ‣ Appendix F Detailed decoding rules and baselines ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we therefore precompute <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))</annotation></semantics></math> once per scorer <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> before
scoring individual candidates.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Scorer-specific entropic value, risk premium, and dispersion</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each scorer <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the scorer-specific empirical entropic value using normalized samples:</p>
<table id="A5.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ -\frac{1}{\beta}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\!\big(-\beta\,\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)\big)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ -\frac{1}{\beta}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp\!\big(-\beta\,\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)\big)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the corresponding empirical mean</p>
<table id="A5.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We define the scorer-specific empirical entropic risk premium as</p>
<table id="A5.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))-\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ \geq\ 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))-\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ \geq\ 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We also define the scorer-specific empirical standard deviation (used as a disagreement proxy) as</p>
<table id="A5.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \sqrt{\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\Big)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\ :=\ \sqrt{\frac{1}{n-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(\tilde{R}_{m,i}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}_{m}(s,y;\bar{R}_{m}(s),\hat{s}_{m}(s))\Big)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Scorer-robust aggregation and decoding rule</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To hedge scorer shift, we aggregate scorer-specific entropic values via a soft worst-case (soft-min) operator with parameter <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y):=-\frac{1}{\gamma}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\!\big(-\gamma\,\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)\big)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y):=-\frac{1}{\gamma}\log\!\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\exp\!\big(-\gamma\,\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)\big)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which satisfies <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\to\min_{m\in[M]}\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\to\min_{m\in[M]}\widehat{V}_{\beta,m}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
For explicit risk control, we aggregate risk premia pessimistically:</p>
<table id="A5.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\ \widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\ \widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta,m}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The scorer-robust risk-constrained decoding rule is then</p>
<table id="A5.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\ \widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\ \widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">or in penalized (Lagrangian) form,</p>
<table id="A5.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\ \widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)-\lambda\,\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}\in\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}\ \widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)-\lambda\,\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Interpretation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The aggregation <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> hedges against worst-case scorers while remaining smooth and stable for finite <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
The pessimistic risk-premium aggregation <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents a candidate from being selected if it is deemed high-risk by any scorer.
When scorer variability reflects genuine preference uncertainty (e.g., validated proxies or ensembles calibrated to human disagreement), this multi-scorer instantiation also promotes reliability under heterogeneous preferences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Detailed decoding rules and baselines</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Candidate set and selection statistics.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given an input <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we sample a fixed candidate set <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from a generator policy <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each candidate <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute an empirical satisfaction mean <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and a dispersion proxy <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>
(see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS8" title="A.8 Selection statistics: empirical mean, dispersion, and CVaR ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> for the exact estimation procedure).
When using CVaR, we additionally compute the empirical lower-tail mean <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{CVaR}}_{\alpha,\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CVaR</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>sel</mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{CVaR}}_{\alpha,\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Full pseudocode for DARC</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> DARC with scorer-robust aggregation (full version)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            prompt <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            candidate set <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}(s)=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}(s)=\{y_{1},\dots,y_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (fixed for all methods)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            scorer family <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textsc{Score}^{(m)}_{\beta}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Score</mtext><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textsc{Score}^{(m)}_{\beta}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{Score}^{(m)}_{\beta}(s,y;\bar{R},\hat{s})\rightarrow(\hat{\mu}_{m},\widehat{V}_{\beta,m},\hat{\sigma}_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Score</mtext><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{Score}^{(m)}_{\beta}(s,y;\bar{R},\hat{s})\rightarrow(\hat{\mu}_{m},\widehat{V}_{\beta,m},\hat{\sigma}_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            aggregation parameter <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (soft worst-case over scorers)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            variant <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\{\textsc{Entropic},\textsc{Tau},\textsc{Eps},\textsc{2nd-Moment (LCB)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Entropic</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Tau</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Eps</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">2nd-Moment (LCB)</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{\textsc{Entropic},\textsc{Tau},\textsc{Eps},\textsc{2nd-Moment (LCB)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and hyperparameters <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\lambda,\tau,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\lambda,\tau,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            selected output <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Optional but recommended) Within-prompt normalization across scorers (selection-time only).</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Precompute pooled normalization constants for each scorer <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> over all candidates <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              Collect raw samples <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{m,i}(s,y_{k})\}_{k\in[K],\,i\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{m,i}(s,y_{k})\}_{k\in[K],\,i\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
