</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Human disagreement on the raw Top-<math id="A8.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> pool (<math id="A8.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>) measured by the maximum across-candidate human rating variance <math id="A8.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
High-disagreement prompts are defined as the top 20% by <math id="A8.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.2 </span>Hyperparameter selection</h3>

<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overview.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report hyperparameters for (i) training-time robust policies (cDPO/rDPO) and (ii) inference-time selection methods and proxy-risk estimation, including DARC and inference-time baselines (DeAL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, MC-Dropout <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gal and Ghahramani, 2016</a>)</cite>, RBoN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jinnai et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Best-of-Poisson/HedgeTune <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khalaf et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and <em id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Caution</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anonymous, 2025</a>)</cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise stated, we use a single fixed set of hyperparameters for all reported results, with no dataset- or split-specific tuning.
All inference-time baselines share the same candidate pools and reward-model preprocessing/truncation for a fair comparison.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Base model and parameter-efficient fine-tuning (cDPO/rDPO).</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All policy and reference models are initialized from <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</span>.
We fine-tune with QLoRA using 4-bit NF4 quantization with double quantization enabled and bf16 compute.
We train LoRA adapters with rank <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}16</annotation></semantics></math>, scaling <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}32</annotation></semantics></math>, dropout <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, and no bias parameters.
We enable gradient checkpointing and disable KV caching during training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">cDPO training.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We optimize the standard DPO objective with inverse-temperature <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and label smoothing <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathrm{ls}}{=}0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>ls</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathrm{ls}}{=}0.10</annotation></semantics></math>.
Unless stated otherwise, we use learning rate <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, per-device batch size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, gradient accumulation <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math> (effective batch size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>), and train for <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> epochs in bf16.
We cap the maximum prompt length at <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> and the maximum response length at <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> (total length <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>1024</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 1024</annotation></semantics></math> tokens), and set the random seed to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">rDPO training.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same initialization, QLoRA/LoRA configuration, and optimization settings as cDPO, but optimize the rDPO objective with label-flip noise parameter <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{flip}}=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>flip</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{flip}}=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and inverse-temperature <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.
The reference model is kept frozen throughout training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference-time candidate pools.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For automated proxy evaluation and inference-time reranking, we generate a fixed candidate pool of size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}16</annotation></semantics></math> per prompt using nucleus sampling with top-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}0.98</annotation></semantics></math> and temperature <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, with at most <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math> newly generated tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward model and proxy-risk statistics.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We score each candidate with the reward model <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Skywork/Skywork-Reward-Llama-3.1-8B-v0.2</span> using maximum input length <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.
To estimate proxy disagreement, we construct <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}{=}8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}{=}8</annotation></semantics></math> style-preserving perturbations per candidate and define the sample set
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{r_{\mathrm{orig}}\}\cup\{r^{(j)}_{\mathrm{aug}}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>orig</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>aug</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{r_{\mathrm{orig}}\}\cup\{r^{(j)}_{\mathrm{aug}}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where each element is the reward model score on the corresponding prompt–response formatting.
We then compute the empirical mean <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, standard deviation <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, and tail metric <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mn>0.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math> as the average of the lowest <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> of samples in <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DARC (entropic) decoding hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our primary decoding rule selects the candidate maximizing the empirical entropic robust value
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log\!\big(\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{r\in\mathcal{S}}\exp(-\beta r)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}=-\frac{1}{\beta}\log\!\big(\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{r\in\mathcal{S}}\exp(-\beta r)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>,
with entropic temperature <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also report two deployment-friendly variants:
(i) <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DARC-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>, which constrains the entropic risk premium <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}=\hat{\mu}-\widehat{V}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}=\hat{\mu}-\widehat{V}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> by a budget <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>; we set <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> to the <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{RP}}{=}0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>RP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{RP}}{=}0.25</annotation></semantics></math> quantile of <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\widehat{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\}_{y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> on each candidate pool and select the feasible candidate with the largest <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DARC-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span>, which forms a near-optimal set in robust value
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y:\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y)\geq\max_{y^{\prime}}\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y^{\prime})-\epsilon_{V}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y:\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y)\geq\max_{y^{\prime}}\widehat{V}_{\beta}(y^{\prime})-\epsilon_{V}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{V}{=}0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{V}{=}0.25</annotation></semantics></math>
and selects the candidate with the smallest <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> (tie-breaking by larger <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Unless otherwise noted, the mainline entropic variant uses the DARC-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> selection rule.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DeAL hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a lightweight and stable DeAL configuration:
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8,\ L=16,\ \gamma=0.05," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8,\ L=16,\ \gamma=0.05,</annotation></semantics></math> and cap the maximum generation length to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\max}=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\max}=512</annotation></semantics></math> new tokens.
Lookahead rollouts are computed with greedy decoding (deterministic rollout; no sampling).
For reward-model inference within DeAL lookahead, we use maximum RM input length <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> and batch size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MC-Dropout uncertainty reranking.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the MC-Dropout baseline, we enable dropout in the reward model at inference time and draw <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}8</annotation></semantics></math> stochastic forward passes per (prompt, candidate), yielding reward samples <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r^{(m)}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compute <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\mathrm{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>MC</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\mathrm{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\mathrm{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>MC</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\mathrm{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mn>0.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> on these samples with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and use the uncertainty-penalized score <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\mathrm{MC}}-\alpha_{\mathrm{MC}}\hat{\sigma}_{\mathrm{MC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>MC</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>MC</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\mathrm{MC}}-\alpha_{\mathrm{MC}}\hat{\sigma}_{\mathrm{MC}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{MC}}{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{MC}}{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RBoN (regularized Best-of-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>) decoding-time reranking.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the RBoN baseline, we rerank the same candidate pool (<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}16</annotation></semantics></math>) using</p>
<table id="A8.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Score}_{\mathrm{RBoN}}(s,y)=r_{\phi}(s,y)+\beta_{\mathrm{RBoN}}\,\overline{\log p_{\mathrm{ref}}}(y\mid s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Score</mi><mi>RBoN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>RBoN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Score}_{\mathrm{RBoN}}(s,y)=r_{\phi}(s,y)+\beta_{\mathrm{RBoN}}\,\overline{\log p_{\mathrm{ref}}}(y\mid s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reward-model score and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\log p_{\mathrm{ref}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\log p_{\mathrm{ref}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the per-token mean log-likelihood under a reference policy <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> (we use the generator policy) to reduce length bias.
We use <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{RBoN}}{=}0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>RBoN</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{RBoN}}{=}0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and compute log-likelihoods with the same maximum length cap (1024 tokens) as reward scoring; due to memory constraints we use a small batch size for log-prob evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Best-of-Poisson (BoP) and HedgeTune.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khalaf et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we implement Best-of-Poisson selection on the same fixed candidate pool (<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}16</annotation></semantics></math>).
For each prompt, we sample <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}\sim\mathrm{Poisson}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Poisson</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}\sim\mathrm{Poisson}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and truncate to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}\leftarrow\min(\max(K^{\prime},1),K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}\leftarrow\min(\max(K^{\prime},1),K)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then select the candidate with the largest reward-model score among a uniformly sampled subset of size <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from the pool
(to avoid positional bias).
As a default, we use <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda{=}12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda{=}12</annotation></semantics></math> and report a global tuning range <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\{4,8,12,16\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\{4,8,12,16\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For HedgeTune, we choose <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> once on a small held-out calibration split (shared across all datasets) and fix it for all reported results,
in line with our no dataset- or split-specific tuning protocol.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><em id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Caution</em>: pessimistic best-of-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> reranking.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement the pessimistic reranking baseline of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anonymous (2025)</a></cite> on the same candidate pool (<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}16</annotation></semantics></math>).
In addition to the reward score <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\phi}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\phi}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, we fit an auxiliary error/atypicality model on in-distribution data and compute an
atypicality penalty <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Candidates are ranked by the pessimistic score
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Score}_{\mathrm{Caution}}(s,y)=r_{\phi}(s,y)-\alpha_{\mathrm{caut}}\,e(s,y)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Score</mi><mi>Caution</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>caut</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Score}_{\mathrm{Caution}}(s,y)=r_{\phi}(s,y)-\alpha_{\mathrm{caut}}\,e(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math>
We use <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{caut}}{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>caut</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{caut}}{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math> by default.
The auxiliary model is trained once and reused across all datasets and splits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Auxiliary error/atypicality model <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> as a supervised classifier over prompt–response pairs.
The input is the concatenation <span id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[PROMPT] <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> [SEP] [RESPONSE] <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math></span>, and the output is a scalar
<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(s,y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(s,y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> interpreted as the probability that <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">atypical</em> under the in-distribution training data.
We use a pretrained Transformer encoder (same backbone family as the reward model for tokenization compatibility) with a single linear head.
Training data is constructed from the in-distribution training split only:</p>
<ul id="A8.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Typical pairs.</span> Ground-truth prompt–response pairs from the training split.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Atypical pairs.</span> (i) <em id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Mismatched</em> pairs formed by pairing each prompt with a response sampled from a different prompt,
and (ii) <em id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">corrupted</em> responses obtained by applying lightweight perturbations to a typical response (random truncation, sentence order
shuffling, and insertion of an unrelated sentence sampled from another example).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We train with binary cross-entropy, using a fixed 1:1 ratio of typical to atypical pairs, early stopping on a held-out validation subset,
and a fixed hyperparameter setting (learning rate, batch size, epochs) shared across all datasets and splits.
At inference time, we compute <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> for each candidate in the pool and apply the above pessimistic reranking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Subset definitions and diagnostics.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For stratified robustness reporting, we define the high-disagreement subset as the top <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> prompts by the baseline (mean Best-of-<math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>) proxy disagreement <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When reporting second-moment baselines or legacy ablations, we additionally include the mean–dispersion score <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}-\lambda\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}-\lambda\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{raw}}{=}5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>raw</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{raw}}{=}5.0</annotation></semantics></math> (and a <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>-scored variant with <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{z}{=}3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{z}{=}3.0</annotation></semantics></math>), used only for diagnostic comparisons.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward model score truncation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For proxy satisfaction samples, we use the reward model’s scalar outputs (logits).
To align with Assumption 3.2 and avoid undue influence from rare outliers, we truncate logits to <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-L,L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-L,L]</annotation></semantics></math>
(we use <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=10</annotation></semantics></math>) before computing <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{n}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{n}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{n}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{n}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}_{\beta}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We choose <math id="A8.SS2.SSS0.Px15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> large enough that truncation is rarely active in practice.
For completeness, Appendix <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Lower-tail (risk) interpretation and uniform empirical LCB under sub-Gaussianity ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a> states an analogous lower-tail interpretation under sub-Gaussianity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T5" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A8.T5.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:73.9pt;vertical-align:-35.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-139.4pt,29.9pt) scale(0.553128552398743,0.553128552398743) ;">
<table id="A8.T5.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Component</span></th>
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters (default)</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Base model</span></th>
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Candidate generation</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}16</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, temperature </span><math id="A8.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.3.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, top-</span><math id="A8.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}0.98</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.3.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, max_new_tokens </span><math id="A8.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reward model scoring</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Skywork/Skywork-Reward-Llama-3.1-8B-v0.2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">(</span><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024a</a><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">)</span></cite></span><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, max length </span><math id="A8.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.4.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, batch size </span><math id="A8.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Proxy disagreement</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}{=}8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">aug</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}{=}8</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> perturbations; samples </span><math id="A8.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{r_{\mathrm{orig}}\}\cup\{r_{\mathrm{aug}}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒮</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">orig</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∪</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">aug</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">aug</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{r_{\mathrm{orig}}\}\cup\{r_{\mathrm{aug}}^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}.</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.5.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; </span><math id="A8.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}=\mathrm{Std}(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒮</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}=\mathrm{Std}(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Proxy tail metric</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">CVaR</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> on </span><math id="A8.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">DARC entropic</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (robust value), </span><math id="A8.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{RP}}{=}0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">RP</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{RP}}{=}0.25</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (DARC-</span><math id="A8.T5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">), </span><math id="A8.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{V}{=}0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">V</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{V}{=}0.25</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (DARC-</span><math id="A8.T5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.7.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">High-disagreement subset</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">top </span><math id="A8.T5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.8.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> prompts by baseline </span><math id="A8.T5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">cDPO training</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">DPO</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="A8.T5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathrm{ls}}{=}0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ls</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathrm{ls}}{=}0.10</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, lr </span><math id="A8.T5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">10</mn><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, epochs </span><math id="A8.T5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, bs </span><math id="A8.T5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.9.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, gas </span><math id="A8.T5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">rDPO training</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="A8.T5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">DPO</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\text{DPO}}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, noise </span><math id="A8.T5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon{=}0.10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon{=}0.10</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, lr </span><math id="A8.T5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">10</mn><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, epochs </span><math id="A8.T5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, bs </span><math id="A8.T5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.10.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, gas </span><math id="A8.T5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T5.3.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T5.3.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LoRA / QLoRA</span></th>
<td id="A8.T5.3.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A8.T5.3.1.11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">4-bit NF4 + double quant + bf16 compute; LoRA </span><math id="A8.T5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}16</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.11.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="A8.T5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}32</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T5.3.1.11.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, dropout </span><math id="A8.T5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Default hyperparameters used in cDPO/rDPO training and inference-time evaluation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.3 </span>Complete metric definitions and computation</h3>

<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> be a prompt and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> a candidate response.
In proxy settings we may use a family of scorers (reward models) <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{R_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{R_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{(m)}_{i}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{(m)}_{i}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> for scalar reward samples returned by scorer <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math> for selection-time samples and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> for held-out evaluation samples
(disjoint to avoid selection–evaluation leakage).
Unless stated otherwise, all reported metrics are computed <em id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">within a fixed scorer</em> <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> on its raw reward scale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt-level evaluation mean.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be held-out reward samples.
We define</p>
<table id="A8.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}}r_{i}(s,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\frac{1}{|\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{\text{eval}}}r_{i}(s,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Disagreement / risk proxy via perturbation sensitivity.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each response <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, generate <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math> style-preserving perturbations <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{y}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{y}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}_{1}:=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}_{1}:=y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under scorer <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y):=R_{m}(s,\tilde{y}_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y):=R_{m}(s,\tilde{y}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> be the reward of perturbation <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</p>
<table id="A8.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{aug}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>aug</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{aug}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{N_{\text{aug}}}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\frac{1}{N_{\text{aug}}}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{N_{\text{aug}}-1}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}\big(u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{aug}}(s,y)\big)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>aug</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sqrt{\frac{1}{N_{\text{aug}}-1}\sum_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}\big(u^{(m)}_{j}(s,y)-\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{aug}}(s,y)\big)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When a scorer-robust selection rule is used, we aggregate disagreement pessimistically at selection time via
<math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}(s,y):=\max_{m\in[M]}\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}_{\text{sel}}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">risk–reward tradeoff score (Tradeoff).</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within scorer <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A8.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed across methods.
For scorer-robust methods, selection uses the aggregated statistics (e.g., <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma,\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>sel</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma,\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>sel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\sigma}_{\text{sel}}</annotation></semantics></math>),
but reporting is performed within each scorer <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid mixing incomparable reward scales.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tail risk: <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}</annotation></semantics></math> over prompts.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a method that outputs one final response <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> per prompt <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, define prompt-level outcome</p>
<table id="A8.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z(s)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s))\quad\text{(or }z(s):=\mathrm{LCB}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s))\text{, specified per table).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>(or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LCB</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>, specified per table).</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z(s)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s))\quad\text{(or }z(s):=\mathrm{LCB}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{\mathcal{Y}}(s))\text{, specified per table).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z(s_{k})\}_{k=1}^{N_{\text{pr}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>pr</mtext></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z(s_{k})\}_{k=1}^{N_{\text{pr}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{pr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>pr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{pr}}</annotation></semantics></math> prompt outcomes and let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{(1)}\leq\cdots\leq z_{(M)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{(1)}\leq\cdots\leq z_{(M)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sorted values.
We define</p>
<table id="A8.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}:=\frac{1}{\lceil 0.1N_{\text{pr}}\rceil}\sum_{k=1}^{\lceil 0.1N_{\text{pr}}\rceil}z_{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>pr</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>pr</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CVaR}_{10\%}:=\frac{1}{\lceil 0.1N_{\text{pr}}\rceil}\sum_{k=1}^{\lceil 0.1N_{\text{pr}}\rceil}z_{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">High-variance (HV) subset evaluation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define a high-variance prompt subset by ranking prompts using the baseline method’s risk proxy (e.g., <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}(s,\hat{y}_{\text{base}}(s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}(s,\hat{y}_{\text{base}}(s))</annotation></semantics></math>) and taking the top <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\%</annotation></semantics></math> prompts (we use <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=20</annotation></semantics></math> unless otherwise stated).
All HV metrics are computed on this fixed subset for every method.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Win/Tie/Loss (W/T/L) across scorers.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given two methods <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, for each prompt <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> define the score difference under a scorer <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A8.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(s):=z_{A}^{R}(s)-z_{B}^{R}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(s):=z_{A}^{R}(s)-z_{B}^{R}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We count a tie if <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{R}(s)|&lt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{R}(s)|&lt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (we use <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\text{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>0.5</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\text{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>; set <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> if not used), otherwise win/loss by the sign of <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We report W/T/L rates over prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Correlation and top-<math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\%</annotation></semantics></math> overlap.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess agreement between two scoring functions <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute Spearman’s rank correlation <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (and optionally Kendall’s <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) between the per-prompt outcomes <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z^{R_{1}}(s)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z^{R_{1}}(s)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z^{R_{2}}(s)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z^{R_{2}}(s)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also report top-<math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\%</annotation></semantics></math> overlap: let <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of prompts in the top <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\%</annotation></semantics></math> according to <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{R}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{R}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>; the overlap is</p>
<table id="A8.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Overlap}_{q\%}(R_{1},R_{2}):=\frac{|\mathcal{T}_{R_{1}}\cap\mathcal{T}_{R_{2}}|}{|\mathcal{T}_{R_{1}}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Overlap</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Overlap}_{q\%}(R_{1},R_{2}):=\frac{|\mathcal{T}_{R_{1}}\cap\mathcal{T}_{R_{2}}|}{|\mathcal{T}_{R_{1}}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metric hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise stated, we use <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}=8</annotation></semantics></math> perturbations per response for estimating robustness statistics, where we include the original response as one sample and draw <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}-1</annotation></semantics></math> style-preserving perturbations.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              Equivalently, we compute statistics over the multiset <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{y}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{y}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{N_{\text{aug}}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{y}_{1}:=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{y}_{1}:=y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
We report the high-disagreement (HV) subset using the top <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=20\%</annotation></semantics></math> prompts ranked by the baseline scorer’s disagreement proxy, and compute Top-<math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\%</annotation></semantics></math> Overlap with <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=20\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the tradeoff metric, we set a fixed weight <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1.99</annotation></semantics></math> across methods and report</p>
<table id="A8.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{\text{eval}}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}(s,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{\text{eval}}(s,y):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical mean RM score (computed on the evaluation split) and <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the disagreement proxy estimated from the perturbation set.
For W/T/L, we treat the RM scores as continuous and set the tie threshold to <math id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{WTL}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>WTL</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{WTL}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A8.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R}(s):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{y})-\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y_{\text{base}}),\qquad\mathrm{WTL}(s)=\begin{cases}\text{W},&amp;\Delta_{R}(s)&gt;0,\\
\text{T},&amp;|\Delta_{R}(s)|\leq 0,\\
\text{L},&amp;\Delta_{R}(s)&lt;0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>WTL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>W</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>T</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>L</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R}(s):=\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,\hat{y})-\hat{\mu}_{\text{eval}}(s,y_{\text{base}}),\qquad\mathrm{WTL}(s)=\begin{cases}\text{W},&amp;\Delta_{R}(s)&gt;0,\\
\text{T},&amp;|\Delta_{R}(s)|\leq 0,\\
\text{L},&amp;\Delta_{R}(s)&lt;0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A8.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.08145v1/bucket_eps_raw_dcvar10.svg" id="A8.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/127;" width="238" height="127"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A8.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Conservative metric exhibits the same bucketed trend.<span id="A8.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Bucketed improvements (vs. base) for a conservative cvar-style score (e.g., <math id="A8.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathrm{CVaR}_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>CVaR</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathrm{CVaR}_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>),
, using the same human-disagreement buckets as Fig. <a href="#A8.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Metric hyperparameters. ‣ H.3 Complete metric definitions and computation ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Bars show mean; error bars denote 95% CIs.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS3.SSS0.Px9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consistent with the Tradeoff results, the conservative cvar-style metric in Fig. <a href="#A8.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Metric hyperparameters. ‣ H.3 Complete metric definitions and computation ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the largest gains in the highest-disagreement bucket, indicating that our improvements are not limited to mean reward but extend to pessimistic/robust criteria that emphasize reliability under preference heterogeneity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.4 </span>Selecting risk controls and practical calibration</h3>

<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overview.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\tau,\lambda,\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\tau,\lambda,\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> on a held-out development set, fixing the candidate set size <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and (when used) the scorer family and normalization protocol (Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Scorer ambiguity and multi-scorer aggregation ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tuning <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We tune <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> via a grid search on the development set to trade off mean quality and robustness metrics (disagreement / tail risk). Unless otherwise specified, we use a single <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> shared across prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Constraint threshold <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> via quantiles.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the constrained decoder (<a href="#S4.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Risk-constrained decoding via an entropic risk premium. ‣ 4.1 From preference maximization to risk controls ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), we set <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> using a quantile rule on the empirical distribution of <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> over candidates:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\mathrm{Quantile}_{q}\big(\{\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Quantile</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\mathrm{Quantile}_{q}\big(\{\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y):y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)\}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> chosen on the development set.
This heuristic keeps the feasible set <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\tau}(s)=\{y:\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\tau}(s)=\{y:\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)\leq\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math> nonempty and controls its typical size across prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Penalty coefficient <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the penalized form (<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Risk-constrained decoding via an entropic risk premium. ‣ 4.1 From preference maximization to risk controls ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), we tune <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> on the development set.
A finite-candidate-set relationship between <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is provided in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS6" title="A.6 Constraint vs. penalty: Lagrangian view (finite candidate set) ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>; in practice, we treat <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> as a direct deployment knob.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choosing <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for near-tie breaking.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We select <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on the development set to trade off robust value and disagreement in (<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ ϵ-rule as a constrained optimization. ‣ 4.2 Practical decoding: ϵ-tie breaking ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), and report sensitivity to <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in the ablations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-scorer setting.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When using <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> scorers, selection operates on the aggregated statistics <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\beta,\gamma}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>RP</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathrm{RP}}_{\beta}(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Scorer-robust decoding (multi-reward models). ‣ 4.3 Multi-scorer robustness ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Scorer ambiguity and multi-scorer aggregation ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>. When <math id="A8.SS4.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>, these reduce to the single-scorer quantities.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.5 </span>Scalarization robustness: absolute ratings vs. pairwise preferences</h3>

<div id="A8.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To bridge our scalar-sample analysis with the common pairwise-preference setting, we verify that our main conclusions are stable under two alternative scalarizations of the same human rating data.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we compare a method-selected response <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{m}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{m}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> against the baseline-selected response <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\text{base}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\text{base}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We collect <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independent human ratings <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}(s,y)\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> on a bounded scale (e.g., 1–10) for each evaluated response <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
Unless stated otherwise, we analyze prompt-level differences and then aggregate over prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">S0: absolute-rating scalarization.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We treat the raw rating as a scalar satisfaction sample,</p>
<table id="A8.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\text{S0}}_{i}(s,m):=r_{i}\!\left(s,y_{m}(s)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>S0</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\text{S0}}_{i}(s,m):=r_{i}\!\left(s,y_{m}(s)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and define the prompt-level mean improvement over the baseline as</p>
<table id="A8.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\text{S0}}(s,m):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))-r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S0</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\text{S0}}(s,m):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))-r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">S1: pairwise (win/tie/loss) scalarization against baseline.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We convert the same ratings into pairwise outcomes against the baseline per annotator:</p>
<table id="A8.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{i}(s,m):=\mathbb{I}\!\left[r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))&gt;r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\right]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{I}\!\left[r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))=r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\right]\in\{0,\tfrac{1}{2},1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mi>𝕀</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(s,m):=\mathbb{I}\!\left[r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))&gt;r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\right]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{I}\!\left[r_{i}(s,y_{m}(s))=r_{i}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\right]\in\{0,\tfrac{1}{2},1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We then define the prompt-level improvement relative to a <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> tie baseline:</p>
<table id="A8.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}(s,m)-\tfrac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S1</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m):=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}(s,m)-\tfrac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S1</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m)</annotation></semantics></math> measures how much the win-rate against the baseline exceeds <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\%</annotation></semantics></math> (with ties counted as half wins).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Win/Tie/Loss aggregation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each scalarization <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\{\Delta^{\text{S0}},\Delta^{\text{S1}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S0</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S1</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\{\Delta^{\text{S0}},\Delta^{\text{S1}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we report prompt-level Win/Tie/Loss counts:</p>
<table id="A8.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{W/T/L}(m)=\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)&gt;0\}\Big|\;\Big/\;\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)=0\}\Big|\;\Big/\;\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)&lt;0\}\Big|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.502em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.502em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{W/T/L}(m)=\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)&gt;0\}\Big|\;\Big/\;\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)=0\}\Big|\;\Big/\;\Big|\{s:\Delta(s,m)&lt;0\}\Big|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We also report the mean improvement <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s}[\Delta(s,m)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s}[\Delta(s,m)]</annotation></semantics></math> over prompts.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">High-disagreement subset.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze where gains concentrate, we define prompt-level human disagreement on the baseline response by</p>
<table id="A8.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\text{base}}(s):=\mathrm{Std}\!\left(\,r_{1}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s)),\ldots,r_{n}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\,\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.382em;" width="1.382em"><mi>Std</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\text{base}}(s):=\mathrm{Std}\!\left(\,r_{1}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s)),\ldots,r_{n}(s,y_{\text{base}}(s))\,\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and select the top <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> prompts by <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{\text{base}}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{\text{base}}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> as the high-disagreement subset.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt-level stability across scalarizations.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we quantify whether the two scalarizations yield consistent prompt-wise improvements by computing the Spearman rank correlation</p>
<table id="A8.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{m}:=\mathrm{Spearman}\!\left(\{\Delta^{\text{S0}}(s,m)\}_{s},\{\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m)\}_{s}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:4.484em;" width="4.484em"><mi>Spearman</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S0</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>S1</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{m}:=\mathrm{Spearman}\!\left(\{\Delta^{\text{S0}}(s,m)\}_{s},\{\Delta^{\text{S1}}(s,m)\}_{s}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A positive and substantial <math id="A8.SS5.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the prompts benefiting from risk-aware selection are largely consistent across absolute-rating and pairwise scalarizations.
Finally, we empirically verify that the key selection trends remain stable across alternative scalarizations of pairwise data (e.g., win-rate vs. fitted scores); see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS14" title="A.14 From pairwise comparisons to scalar samples ‣ Appendix A Additional Theoretical Details ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>.</p>
</div>
