S0 uses raw scalar satisfaction ratings. S1 converts ratings into pairwise preferences against the base response
(win = 1, tie = 0.5, loss = 0) per annotator, then averages across annotators.
Trends are consistent under both scalarizations, especially on high-disagreement prompts.
(Additional prompt-level stability: Spearman correlation of per-prompt <math id="A8.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> between S0 and S1 is
0.595/0.665 overall and 0.688/0.764 on the high-disagreement subset for raw/eps, respectively.)</figcaption>
</figure>
