<section id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference latency.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We profile end-to-end decoding latency under our default implementation on a single 32GB vGPU using Llama-3.1-8B for candidate generation and Skywork-Reward for scoring.
Disagreement estimation incurs additional reward-model forward passes over style-preserving perturbations, controlled by <math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Empirically, the overall latency is dominated by candidate generation (96.5–99.7% of total time), while augmentation scoring accounts for only 1.6–3.2% when <math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}=4</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, compared with <math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, our default <math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{aug}}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{aug}}=4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A8.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> increase end-to-end latency by only 1.54% and 1.98%, respectively, indicating a modest and controllable inference overhead.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.7 </span>Additional proxy validity analysis</h3>

<figure id="A8.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.08145v1/bucket_trend_lcb_dual.svg" id="A8.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/100;" width="238" height="100"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A8.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A8.F6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Bucketed predictive validity of the disagreement proxy.<span id="A8.F6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We partition prompts into quintiles (Q1–Q5) by disagreement of the <em id="A8.F6.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">baseline</em> candidate, using either human disagreement (left) or proxy disagreement (right).
We then report the improvement in <math id="A8.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Tradeoff</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}</annotation></semantics></math> of DARC-<math id="A8.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> over the mean-only baseline, within each bucket.
Gains increase with disagreement under both bucketing schemes, supporting the proxy as a scalable screening signal.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.8 </span>Additional Robustness to Proxy Reliability</h3>

<section id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Motivation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess robustness when such proxies are less aligned with human disagreement, we perform an <em id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">error-bucket</em> analysis that stratifies prompts by the mismatch between proxy disagreement and human disagreement, and compares performance within each bucket.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Definitions.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">base</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the baseline response selected by mean Best-of-<math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define:</p>
<table id="A8.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sigma_{\text{proxy}}\!\left(s_{i},y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">base</mtext></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sigma_{\text{proxy}}\!\left(s_{i},y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d^{\text{human}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d^{\text{human}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\sigma_{\text{human}}\!\left(s_{i},y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">base</mtext></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\sigma_{\text{human}}\!\left(s_{i},y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A8.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E83.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\left|d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}-d^{\text{human}}_{i}\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\left|d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}-d^{\text{human}}_{i}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>proxy</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{proxy}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the proxy disagreement estimate used in our pipeline (computed from the underlying proxy/scorer procedure), and
<math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{\text{human}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>human</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{\text{human}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard deviation of <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independent judge ratings for the <em id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> baseline response <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">base</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\textsc{base}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on prompt <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
(using the same rating protocol as in the main human-loop evaluation).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bucketing protocol.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We form <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> error buckets using <em id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">quantile-based bin edges</em> of <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Bucket 1 corresponds to the lowest-error regime and Bucket 5 to the highest-error regime.
Due to ties in <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near bin boundaries, bucket sizes are not exactly equal.
We report results per bucket, emphasizing Bucket 5 as the <em id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">worst proxy-reliability</em> regime.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metric (Tradeoff).</h4>

<div id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each method <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and prompt <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we aggregate <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> judge ratings into a mean <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{i,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{i,m}</annotation></semantics></math> and standard deviation <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}_{i,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}_{i,m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and compute</p>
<table id="A8.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{i,m}:=\hat{\mu}_{i,m}-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}_{i,m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{i,m}:=\hat{\mu}_{i,m}-\lambda\,\hat{\sigma}_{i,m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is the same value used in our main human-loop analysis (reported alongside results).
We then average <math id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{i,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}_{i,m}</annotation></semantics></math> within each bucket and compare to the baseline.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS8.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the proposed method improves (or at least does not degrade) Tradeoff even in Bucket 5, this suggests that gains are not solely driven by strong alignment between the proxy disagreement signal and human disagreement.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T8" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A8.T8.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A8.T8.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><span id="A8.T8.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Error bucket</span></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><math id="A8.T8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><math id="A8.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e]\!\pm\!\mathrm{Std}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">e</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.102em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.102em">±</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">Std</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e]\!\pm\!\mathrm{Std}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><span id="A8.T8.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">TO<span id="A8.T8.3.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> (Base)</span></span></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><math id="A8.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T8.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> DeAL</span></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><math id="A8.T8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T8.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> RBoN</span></th>
<th id="A8.T8.3.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><math id="A8.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A8.T8.3.1.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;"> DARC-<math id="A8.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A8.T8.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T8.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.2pt 3.5pt;"><span id="A8.T8.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">Q0–20%</span></th>
