<tr id="A8.T14.3.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T14.3.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.14.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">DARC-<math id="A8.T14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="A8.T14.3.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.14.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.41</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.14.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.14.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">4.16</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.14.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.14.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-2.91</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.14.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.14.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.12</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T14.3.15" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T14.3.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.15.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">DARC-<math id="A8.T14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="A8.T14.3.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.15.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.49</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.15.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.15.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">3.67</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.15.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.15.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">-1.85</span></td>
<td id="A8.T14.3.15.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;"><span id="A8.T14.3.15.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5.19</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Additional results on <span id="A8.T14.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct</span>. We report mean reward (Avg<math id="A8.T14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>), disagreement risk (Avg<math id="A8.T14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>), Tradeoff (computed with the same <math id="A8.T14.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> as in the main experiments), and prompt-level tail robustness (CVaR<sub id="A8.T14.15" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A8.T14.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">10%</span></sub>). “High-Variance” denotes the top 20% prompts ranked by baseline disagreement under mean Best-of-<math id="A8.T14.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.13 </span>Style-preserving perturbations for disagreement estimation</h3>

<div id="A8.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To estimate the augmentation-based disagreement proxy <math id="A8.SS13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}^{\mathrm{sel}}_{\mathrm{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>aug</mi><mi>sel</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}^{\mathrm{sel}}_{\mathrm{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct
<math id="A8.SS13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A8.SS13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">style-preserving</em> perturbations of each candidate response <math id="A8.SS13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for a fixed prompt <math id="A8.SS13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
Concretely, for each <math id="A8.SS13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> we generate perturbed variants <math id="A8.SS13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}</annotation></semantics></math> using a rewriting model
<math id="A8.SS13.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., the same LLM backbone used for generation, or a separate paraphrasing model).</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rewrite prompt.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We instruct <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> to produce meaning-preserving paraphrases with only surface-form changes:</p>
<blockquote id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Rewrite Instruction.<span id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Given the prompt and a candidate response, rewrite the response while preserving its meaning.
Only change wording, phrasing, or formatting. Do <em id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> add, remove, or alter facts; do <em id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> change any numbers,
dates, named entities, URLs, or citations. Keep the tone and overall style similar. Keep the length within <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 10\%</annotation></semantics></math>.
Output only the rewritten response (no preamble).</span></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampling and filtering.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,y)</annotation></semantics></math> we sample rewrites from <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> using temperature <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and top-<math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> (we fix the random seed for
reproducibility). We accept a rewrite <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> if it passes all of the following checks:
(i) it satisfies the length constraint; (ii) it does not change any numerals, dates, or detected named entities compared
to <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> (simple string-based checks); and (iii) it is not a duplicate of an existing variant (exact-match).
If a sampled rewrite fails, we resample until obtaining <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math> accepted variants or reaching a maximum of
<math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> attempts; if the cap is reached, we use all accepted variants obtained so far.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scoring and disagreement proxy.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each scorer <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain score samples by evaluating each accepted variant:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{m,i}(s,y)\;:=\;\mathrm{RM}_{m}\!\bigl(s,y^{(i)}\bigr),\qquad i\in[n_{\mathrm{aug}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>RM</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{m,i}(s,y)\;:=\;\mathrm{RM}_{m}\!\bigl(s,y^{(i)}\bigr),\qquad i\in[n_{\mathrm{aug}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We then compute the augmentation-based disagreement proxy as the empirical standard deviation across perturbations,</p>
<table id="A8.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}^{\mathrm{sel}}_{\mathrm{aug}}(s,y)\;:=\;\max_{m\in[M]}\sqrt{\frac{1}{n_{\mathrm{aug}}-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}\Bigl(R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s,y)\Bigr)^{2}},\qquad\bar{R}_{m}(s,y):=\frac{1}{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}R_{m,i}(s,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>aug</mi><mi>sel</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>aug</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}^{\mathrm{sel}}_{\mathrm{aug}}(s,y)\;:=\;\max_{m\in[M]}\sqrt{\frac{1}{n_{\mathrm{aug}}-1}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}\Bigl(R_{m,i}(s,y)-\bar{R}_{m}(s,y)\Bigr)^{2}},\qquad\bar{R}_{m}(s,y):=\frac{1}{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}\sum_{i=1}^{n_{\mathrm{aug}}}R_{m,i}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which matches the worst-case aggregation used in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ F.1 Full pseudocode for DARC ‣ Appendix F Detailed decoding rules and baselines ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Eps variant).
When <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the outer <math id="A8.SS13.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>max</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max</annotation></semantics></math> can be omitted.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.14 </span>Tradeoff metric weight: choice and sensitivity</h3>

<section id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Definition.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within scorer <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the risk–reward tradeoff score</p>
<table id="A8.E86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;-\;\lambda_{\text{eval}}\,\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;:=\;\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)\;-\;\lambda_{\text{eval}}\,\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an evaluation scalarization weight (fixed across methods) and is distinct from the
decoding penalty parameter used in the inference-time objectives (e.g., Eq. (<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Risk-constrained decoding via an entropic risk premium. ‣ 4.1 From preference maximization to risk controls ‣ 4 Disagreement-Aware Risk-Constrained Decoding ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>)).
For scorer-robust methods, selection uses aggregated statistics, but reporting is performed within each scorer <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>
to avoid mixing incomparable reward scales.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choice of <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We set <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}=\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}=\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (used in all main tables) following a simple scale-matching heuristic on a
held-out validation split. Specifically, we choose <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the median magnitudes of the reward and the penalty terms are comparable:</p>
<table id="A8.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A8.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{median}\!\left(|\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)|\right)\;\approx\;\lambda_{0}\cdot\mathrm{median}\!\left(\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.167em;" width="3.167em"><mi>median</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.167em;" width="3.167em"><mi>median</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{median}\!\left(|\hat{\mu}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}(s,y)|\right)\;\approx\;\lambda_{0}\cdot\mathrm{median}\!\left(\hat{\sigma}^{(m)}(s,y)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">computed after applying the same preprocessing (e.g., truncation) used for evaluation.
This data-driven heuristic yields <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}\approx 1.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}\approx 1.99</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sensitivity to <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess robustness, we sweep <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> over a log-spaced grid around <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
(e.g., <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.5\lambda_{0},\lambda_{0},2\lambda_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.5\lambda_{0},\lambda_{0},2\lambda_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>)
and recompute <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Tradeoff</mi><mtext>eval</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Tradeoff}^{(m)}_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each method. Table <a href="#A8.T15" title='Table 15 ‣ Sensitivity to 𝜆_"eval". ‣ H.14 Tradeoff metric weight: choice and sensitivity ‣ Appendix H Experiments ‣ DARC: Disagreement-Aware Alignment via Risk-Constrained Decoding' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>
summarizes the resulting ranks (per scorer <math id="A8.SS14.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>) at representative weights, confirming that the relative improvements of DARC are robust to the specific choice of the scalarization weight.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A8.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Sensitivity of the Tradeoff metric to the evaluation weight <math id="A8.T15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We report the method’s rank (lower is better) under different scalarization weights (<math id="A8.T15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}=1.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}=1.99</annotation></semantics></math>). DARC variants consistently outperform baselines across a wide range of risk preferences.</figcaption>
<table id="A8.T15.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A8.T15.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T15.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A8.T15.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></th>
<th id="A8.T15.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A8.T15.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rank@<math id="A8.T15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A8.T15.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A8.T15.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rank@<math id="A8.T15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="A8.T15.7.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A8.T15.7.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rank@<math id="A8.T15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A8.T15.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A8.T15.7.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A8.T15.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">DARC-<math id="A8.T15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<td id="A8.T15.7.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A8.T15.7.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1</span></td>
<td id="A8.T15.7.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A8.T15.7.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1</span></td>
<td id="A8.T15.7.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A8.T15.7.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A8.T15.7.3" class="ltx_tr">
